    "stac_version": "1.1.0",
    "description": "The absorbing properties of UV radiation of lichen phenols agree with their\nphotoprotector capacity determined by in vivo and in vitro methods. The\nphotostability that characterizes these compounds makes it possible to study\nthe relations between the UV absorbers  and ozone levels in different time\nscales. Usnic acid is the most frequent UV-B absorber in antarctic lichens. In\nNeuropogon aurantiaco-ater (Jacq) I.M. Lamb. and Ramalina terebrata Hook. et\nTayl., collected in Antarctica over a period of 30 years, the highest\nconcentrations of usnic acid were observed when  ozone diminished to critical\nvalues.",
